  "summary": "The loss reproduces, but the card's mechanism is partly falsified. Measured on origin/main 62597c5 with the real FileField, form renderer and react-hook-form (only the upload transport deferred): the upload is NOT aborted by the step unmount, and its settle DOES land. RHF 7.85's Controller onChange re-registers a field it no longer tracks and writes the value, so a Create pressed after the settle stored attachment=file_123. What the unmount ended was the widget's in-flight REPORT, through the unmount release in useUploadingScopeReport. The objectui#10166 final-commit gate then read false while the upload was still running, and a Create pressed before the settle wrote {name:'Alice'} with no attachment and reported success. The repair is on the producer side in @object-ui/fields. A new module-internal useUploadingScopeHold (not exported from the package entry) lets FileField and ImageField (pick and crop) hold the uploading scope for the upload's own lifetime: taken when the upload starts, released in the finally after onChange hands the value over, whether or not the widget is still mounted. Next is not gated and nothing new is rendered: on the last step, Create shows the existing #10166 'Uploading…' label and reason until the upload settles, then stores the file. TabbedForm was measured and does not share the shape (its panels are forceMount; the gate saw the upload after a tab switch), so it is untouched. WizardForm.tsx changes one comment only. The #10166 pin comment in uploadInFlightSave.test.tsx said the value 'never lands in formData at all'; that was measured false and the comment is corrected. The assignee was already os-bill (set by the PM); I did not touch it.",
